# Test: ze doctor --json reports unavailable BGP listener
# VALIDATES: AC-5 BGP local address that cannot bind emits doctor-bgp-listen.
#
# The family carries `prefix { maximum }` because the BGP engine requires it
# ("family ipv4/unicast: prefix maximum is mandatory and must be > 0",
# PeersFromConfigTree). Without it this fixture was a config the daemon refuses
# to start on, and the test still asserted exit 0 -- which passed only because
# `ze doctor` never ran the engine's peer resolution. It does now
# (checkBGPPeerConfig, internal/component/doctor/checks_config.go), so an
# engine-invalid fixture is an error diagnostic and a non-zero exit. Fixing the
# config keeps this test about what it is named for: the listener probe.

tmpfs=bgp-listen.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
    router-id 1.2.3.4
    session {
        asn {
            local 65000
        }
    }
    peer peer1 {
        connection {
            local {
                ip 203.0.113.254
            }
            remote {
                ip 192.0.2.1
            }
        }
        session {
            asn {
                remote 65001
            }
            family {
                ipv4/unicast {
                    prefix {
                        maximum 10000
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze doctor --json bgp-listen.conf
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=doctor-bgp-listen
expect=stdout:contains=203.0.113.254
